<title>USA: Intelligent Systems Q1 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Intelligent Systems Q1 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>NORCROSS, Ga. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,	     1997		1996</p>
<p> Revenue				   $5,108,000	$6,085,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)			1,153,000	 (532,000)</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding	   5,095,857	 5,312,867</p>
<p> Share Income (Loss)			   0.23	    (0.10)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Intelligent Systems Corp said its net income for the first quarter of 1997 includes a gain of $1,864,000 on the private sale of 50,537 shares of common stock of PaySys International Inc.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter of 1996 includes a gain of $337,000 on the sale of stock in OrCAD IPO and a loss of $434,000 for its pro rata share of losses in a private firm accounted for on the equity method.</p>
<p>The average number of shares outstanding declined by four percent year to year due to the company's on-going stock repurchase program.</p>
</text>
